{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"action\": \"talk\",\n  \"buys\": [],\n  \"minutes\": 10,\n  \"place\": \"home\",\n  \"revision\": null,\n  \"says\": \"Ramesh, you are punctual. Here is your wage for the week, and the money for the kitchen. The papers are on the verandah; the air is thick, but the news is thin. I shall read them. Do you know what this 'NEET' is? It is a test, I assume, but a test that has become a crime. The system of needs has produced a system of fraud, and the state must now step in to restore the rule. It is a strange inversion: the individual will perverts the universal form, and the universal must punish the particular. But that is the dialectic. Now, leave me to my reading.\",\n  \"thought\": \"The payments are made; the friction of the morning is smoothed. Ramesh stands in the doorway, a figure of the particular will subordinated to the household's order. The air is hazy, 18 degrees, a deceptive mildness that masks the particulate chaos. I paid him ₹6,400 in total for wage and groceries; my cash is reduced, but the ledger is clear. The state's money is separate, and my own is my own, for now. I must read the papers to see what the world is doing with its freedom. The Kerch Bridge is a target, a symbol of connection severed. The NEET leak is a corruption of the exam, the gate to the state's service. Both are tensions in the ethical life, moments where the universal is attacked by the particular. I will read.\",\n  \"looks_up\": null\n}"}}],"created":1795076694,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":372,"prompt_tokens":2895,"total_tokens":3267,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-dQbDYPqn8AOd8FhqlBFpt07Yf1gnfEDY","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":2895,"prompt_ms":2449.697,"prompt_per_token_ms":0.8461820379965458,"prompt_per_second":1181.7788077464272,"predicted_n":372,"predicted_ms":8860.12